<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait import payments fall in Jan month/month.</title>
<headline>Kuwait import payments fall in Jan month/month.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Payments made by banks in Kuwait to finance imports fell to 111.8 million dinars in January from 135.1 million in December, a Central Bank monthly bulletin said.</p>
<p>The payments were 164.8 million dinars in January 1996.</p>
<p>			   Figures in millions of dinars</p>
<p>					Jan	   Dec	 Jan '96</p>
<p>Documentary LCs		   81.0	  98.5	125.8</p>
<p>Bills for collection	    16.1	  19.6	 18.5</p>
<p>Other payment orders	    14.7	  17.1	 20.5</p>
<p>The relative importance of the U.S. dollar in the financing rose to 60.5 percent in January from 59.6 in December. That of the Japanese yen fell to 7.6 percent from 12.6 percent.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in figures are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.303 dinar)</p>
</text>
